%S A400129 0,0,0,0,0,25,260,3423,49754,810692,14283706,266571436,5191329618
%N A400129 Number of unlabeled connected planar simple graphs G on n vertices for which there exist a vertex v of degree 5 and a proper 4-coloring of G-v in which all four colors occur on the neighbors of v.
%C A400129 The property holds if there exists a vertex v of degree 5 and a proper 4-coloring of G-v satisfying the stated condition. It is invariant under graph relabeling.
%C A400129 Terms are from exhaustive computation. The n=13 computation covered all 5942258308 connected planar graphs in 4096 shards with identical searcher and generator provenance.
%H A400129 E. Gethner et al., <a href="https://doi.org/10.2140/involve.2009.2.249">How False Is Kempe's Proof of the Four Color Theorem? Part II</a>, Involve 2 (2009), 249-265.
%H A400129 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/KempeChain.html">Kempe Chain</a>.
%H A400129 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Kempe-KittellColoringAlgorithm.html">Kempe-Kittell Coloring Algorithm</a>.
%H A400129 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/KempesColoringAlgorithm.html">Kempe's Coloring Algorithm</a>.
%H A400129 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/PlanarConnectedGraph.html">Planar Connected Graph</a>.
%Y A400129 Cf. A003094 (all unlabeled connected planar simple graphs).
%Y A400129 Cf. A400130 (graphs for which some such coloring defeats every standard immediate Kempe repair).
